fuxi: 0125 -- sweetfb_copy: use the CPU copy path when the MDP one lies

The panel shows a stale console frame while the compositor reports 9000 swaps: two grabs
20 s apart differ by 21 pixels out of 162000.  directPresent() hands the surface to the
display controller and returns success, so present() returns early and the CPU copy path
below -- which writes into the buffer the panel is demonstrably scanning -- never runs.

sweetfb_copy=1 skips the early return and forces the copy path.  With sweetfb_noconsole=1
already muting console repaints, this is the combination that should put the composited UI
on the panel instead of a frozen boot log.

Harness: applied=124 skipped=0.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -520,6 +520,21 @@
 {
 	uint32_t mask = get32(rec, 0x104);
 
+	/*
+	 * The MDP path teaches the display controller to scan out the composited
+	 * surface, and on this port it reports success while the panel keeps showing
+	 * whatever was in the boot framebuffer: 9000 swaps, a frames-identical panel.
+	 * sweetfb_copy=1 skips it and uses the CPU copy path below, which writes into
+	 * the buffer the panel is demonstrably scanning.
+	 */
+	{
+		int force_copy = 0;
+
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_copy", &force_copy, sizeof(force_copy));
+		if (force_copy) {
+			goto copy_path;
+		}
+	}
 	if (directPresent(rec)) {
 		if (!fConsolePaused) {
 			int quiet = 0;
@@ -530,6 +545,7 @@
 		}
 		return;
 	}
+copy_path:
 	/* copy path: make sure the MDP shows the boot framebuffer we copy into */
 	if (fVig0 != NULL && fScanPhys != fBootSrc) {
 		scanFrom(fBootSrc, fBootStride);
